IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nz-interpretation-time`

-- Legislation Act 2019 (New Zealand) -- LAYER 1: PART 5, PARLIAMENT'S OVERSIGHT OF SECONDARY LEGISLATION (ss 113 to 127).
-- s 113 (purpose) creates no rule. Part 4 (ss 101 to 112, disclosure requirements) is a list of headings in the deposited text, with no body: see the coverage table in NOTES.md.
-- The sitting days of the House are not fixed by the Act: they are a supplied calendar (a LIST OF DATE, any order). Schedule 3 (presentation and disallowance exemptions) and Schedule 4
-- (what must be confirmed) are tables the deposited text shows only in part; whether an exemption or a listing applies is taken as an input in each rule below.
-- A "day" here is a whole calendar day; a deadline stated as "the close of" a day is that day (nz-interpretation-time.l4, s 54 and s 56).

§ `Section 114 -- Secondary legislation must be presented to House of Representatives`

-- src:778 | 114 Secondary legislation must be presented to House of Representatives
-- src:779 | The relevant Minister must present secondary legislation to the House of Representatives in accordance with the House’s rules and practice.
-- src:780 | However,—
-- src:781 | if a presentation exemption applies to secondary legislation (or a part of secondary legislation) under Schedule 3, this requirement does not apply to that legislation or part; and
-- src:782 | see also section 161A of the Local Government Act 2002, which provides that this requirement does not apply to secondary legislation made by a local authority or a council-controlled organisation unless the empowering legislation (or other legislation) expressly requires presentation to the House of Representatives.
-- The relevant Minister must present secondary legislation to the House in accordance with the House's rules and practice. However this does not apply if a presentation exemption applies under Schedule 3, nor (section 161A of the Local
-- Government Act 2002, a borrowed rule) to secondary legislation made by a local authority or council-controlled organisation unless the empowering legislation (or other legislation) expressly requires presentation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 114 (src:778) (src:779-782)
GIVEN `a presentation exemption applies under Schedule 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made by a local authority or a council-controlled organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `legislation expressly requires presentation to the House` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the relevant Minister must present the secondary legislation to the House` `a presentation exemption applies under Schedule 3` `it is made by a local authority or a council-controlled organisation` `legislation expressly requires presentation to the House` MEANS
        (NOT `a presentation exemption applies under Schedule 3`)
    AND ((NOT `it is made by a local authority or a council-controlled organisation`) OR `legislation expressly requires presentation to the House`)

§ `Section 115 -- All secondary legislation subject to disallowance, with limited exceptions`

-- src:784 | 115 All secondary legislation subject to disallowance, with limited exceptions
-- src:785 | This subpart applies to secondary legislation other than—
-- src:786 | secondary legislation made by resolution of the House of Representatives; or
-- src:787 | secondary legislation made under the Royal prerogative; or
-- src:788 | a bylaw as defined in section 2 of the Bylaws Act 1910; or
-- src:789 | secondary legislation to which a disallowance exemption applies under Schedule 3.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 115 (src:784) (src:785-789)
GIVEN `it is made by resolution of the House of Representatives` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made under the Royal prerogative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a bylaw as defined in section 2 of the Bylaws Act 1910` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a disallowance exemption applies under Schedule 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the disallowance subpart applies to the secondary legislation` `it is made by resolution of the House of Representatives` `it is made under the Royal prerogative` `it is a bylaw as defined in section 2 of the Bylaws Act 1910` `a disallowance exemption applies under Schedule 3` MEANS
        (NOT `it is made by resolution of the House of Representatives`)
    AND (NOT `it is made under the Royal prerogative`)
    AND (NOT `it is a bylaw as defined in section 2 of the Bylaws Act 1910`)
    AND (NOT `a disallowance exemption applies under Schedule 3`)

§ `Section 116 -- House of Representatives may disallow secondary legislation by resolution`

-- src:792 | Legislation disallowed by a resolution ceases to have effect on the later of—
-- src:793 | the passing of the resolution; and
-- src:794 | any date stated in the resolution as the date on which the legislation ceases to have effect.
-- Legislation disallowed by a resolution ceases to have effect on the later of the passing of the resolution and any date stated in the resolution as the date on which the legislation ceases to have effect.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 116(2) (src:792-794)
GIVEN `the day the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
      `the date stated in the resolution` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day legislation disallowed by resolution ceases to have effect` `the day the resolution is passed` `the date stated in the resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date stated in the resolution`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day the resolution is passed`
    WHEN JUST stated THEN IF stated LESS THAN `the day the resolution is passed` THEN `the day the resolution is passed` ELSE stated

-- (1) The House of Representatives may, by resolution, disallow any secondary legislation, or provision of secondary legislation, to which this subpart applies.
-- src:791 | The House of Representatives may, by resolution, disallow any secondary legislation, or provision of secondary legislation, to which this subpart applies.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 116(1) (src:791)
GIVEN `this subpart applies to the secondary legislation or provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the House of Representatives may disallow the secondary legislation or provision by resolution` `this subpart applies to the secondary legislation or provision` MEANS
    `this subpart applies to the secondary legislation or provision`

§ `Section 117 -- Secondary legislation disallowed if House of Representatives does not dispose of motion to disallow`

-- src:805 | In this section, the deadline is the close of the 21st sitting day after the giving of the notice of motion.
-- (3) The deadline is the close of the 21st sitting day after the giving of the notice of motion. The notice is given on a day; the sitting days counted are those strictly after it (s 54, Item 2: "after" starts the next day).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 117(3) (src:805)
GIVEN `the day the notice of motion is given` IS A DATE
      `the sitting days of the House` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the deadline for a notice of motion to disallow given on` `the day the notice of motion is given` `counting the sitting days` `the sitting days of the House` MEANS
    `the nth sitting day after` 21 `counting from` `the day the notice of motion is given` `searching` 400 `more days in` `the sitting days of the House`

-- Helper for sitting days: the nth day in the list that lies strictly after a day, stepping a day at a time for at most `steps` days; NOTHING if the list does not reach that far.
-- src:80 | sitting day means a sitting day of the House of Representatives.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 5(1), definition of sitting day (src:80)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      from IS A DATE
      steps IS A NUMBER
      `the sitting days of the House` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the nth sitting day after` n `counting from` from `searching` steps `more days in` `the sitting days of the House` MEANS
    IF steps LESS THAN 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF n LESS THAN 1
         THEN JUST from
         ELSE IF any (GIVEN sitting YIELD sitting EQUALS (from PLUS 1)) `the sitting days of the House`
              THEN `the nth sitting day after` (n MINUS 1) `counting from` (from PLUS 1) `searching` (steps MINUS 1) `more days in` `the sitting days of the House`
              ELSE `the nth sitting day after` n `counting from` (from PLUS 1) `searching` (steps MINUS 1) `more days in` `the sitting days of the House`

-- Helper for section 117(1): an event that never happens, or happens after the deadline (the close of its day), is not "before the deadline".
GIVEN event IS A MAYBE DATE
      deadline IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the event on` event `is not on or before` deadline MEANS
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST happened THEN happened GREATER THAN deadline

-- (1) disallowed if a member of the Committee gives notice of a motion to disallow it and none of the following happens before the deadline: the notice is withdrawn; the House disposes of the motion; Parliament is dissolved or expires.
-- "Before the deadline" where the deadline is the close of a day: an event on that day, or earlier, is before the close of the deadline.
-- src:796 | Secondary legislation, or a provision of secondary legislation, to which this subpart applies is disallowed if—
-- src:801 | Parliament is dissolved or expires.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 117(1) (src:796-801)
GIVEN `a Committee member gave notice of a motion to disallow it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deadline` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice was withdrawn` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the House disposed of the motion` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day Parliament was dissolved or expired` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the secondary legislation is disallowed under section 117` `a Committee member gave notice of a motion to disallow it` `the deadline` `the day the notice was withdrawn` `the day the House disposed of the motion` `the day Parliament was dissolved or expired` MEANS
        `a Committee member gave notice of a motion to disallow it`
    AND `the event on` `the day the notice was withdrawn` `is not on or before` `the deadline`
    AND `the event on` `the day the House disposed of the motion` `is not on or before` `the deadline`
    AND `the event on` `the day Parliament was dissolved or expired` `is not on or before` `the deadline`

-- (2) Legislation disallowed under this section ceases to have effect on the later of the deadline and any date stated in the notice of motion as the date on which the legislation ceases to have effect.
-- src:802 | Legislation disallowed under this section ceases to have effect on the later of—
-- src:804 | any date stated in the notice of motion as the date on which the legislation ceases to have effect.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 117(2) (src:802-804)
GIVEN `the deadline` IS A DATE
      `the date stated in the notice of motion` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day legislation disallowed under section 117 ceases to have effect` `the deadline` `the date stated in the notice of motion` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date stated in the notice of motion`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the deadline`
    WHEN JUST stated THEN IF stated LESS THAN `the deadline` THEN `the deadline` ELSE stated

§ `Section 118 -- Effect of disallowance on legislation`

DECLARE `Whether earlier legislation is revived` IS ONE OF
    `Revived as it was immediately before it was amended, repealed or revoked: section 118 or 125 alters section 32`
    `Not revived: section 32(2) applies`

-- src:806 | 118 Effect of disallowance on legislation
-- src:807 | If secondary legislation, or a provision of secondary legislation, is disallowed under section 116 or 117, the following applies:
-- src:808 | the disallowance has the same effect as a revocation of the secondary legislation or provision (except as set out in this section):
-- src:809 | any other legislation that was previously amended, repealed, or revoked by the legislation or provision is restored or revived as it was immediately before it was amended, repealed, or revoked:
-- src:810 | the restoration or revival takes effect at the time the disallowed legislation ceases to have effect.
-- src:811 | This section alters the effect of section 32 (which relates to the effect of repeal generally).
-- If secondary legislation or a provision is disallowed under section 116 or 117 (or revoked under section 123 as unconfirmed legislation, section 125(1)(b)), other legislation previously amended, repealed or revoked by it is restored or revived as it was immediately before
-- and the restoration or revival takes effect at the time the disallowed legislation ceases to have effect. Otherwise the repeal of legislation does not revive what it had repealed (section 32(2)).
-- src:842 | any other legislation that was previously amended, repealed, or revoked by the unconfirmed legislation is restored or revived (as it was immediately before it was amended, repealed, or revoked); and
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 118 and s 125(1)(b) (src:806) (src:807-811) (src:842)
GIVEN `it was disallowed under section 116 or 117` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was revoked by section 123 as unconfirmed legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether earlier legislation is revived`
`whether legislation previously amended, repealed or revoked by the later legislation is revived` `it was disallowed under section 116 or 117` `it was revoked by section 123 as unconfirmed legislation` MEANS
    IF `it was disallowed under section 116 or 117` OR `it was revoked by section 123 as unconfirmed legislation`
    THEN `Revived as it was immediately before it was amended, repealed or revoked: section 118 or 125 alters section 32`
    ELSE `Not revived: section 32(2) applies`

-- src:808 | the disallowance has the same effect as a revocation of the secondary legislation or provision (except as set out in this section):
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 118(1)(a) (src:808)
GIVEN `it was disallowed under section 116 or 117` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the disallowance has the same effect as a revocation` `it was disallowed under section 116 or 117` MEANS
    `it was disallowed under section 116 or 117`

-- src:810 | the restoration or revival takes effect at the time the disallowed legislation ceases to have effect.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 118(1)(c) (src:810)
GIVEN `the day the disallowed legislation ceases to have effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the restoration or revival takes effect` `the day the disallowed legislation ceases to have effect` MEANS
    `the day the disallowed legislation ceases to have effect`

§ `Section 119 -- House of Representatives may amend or replace secondary legislation`

-- src:814 | The amendment or replacement takes effect on the later of—
-- src:815 | the 28th day after a copy of the resolution is published; and
-- src:816 | any date stated in the resolution as the date on which it takes effect.
-- (2) The amendment or replacement takes effect on the later of the 28th day after a copy of the resolution is published and any date stated in the resolution as the date on which it takes effect.
-- The 28th day after the publication day: the 28 days start the day after (s 54, Item 2), so it is the publication day plus 28.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 119(2) (src:814-816)
GIVEN `the day a copy of the resolution is published` IS A DATE
      `the date stated in the resolution` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day an amendment or replacement by resolution takes effect` `the day a copy of the resolution is published` `the date stated in the resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date stated in the resolution`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day a copy of the resolution is published` PLUS 28
    WHEN JUST stated THEN IF stated LESS THAN (`the day a copy of the resolution is published` PLUS 28) THEN `the day a copy of the resolution is published` PLUS 28 ELSE stated

-- (3) Secondary legislation that is amended or replaced by resolution may be disallowed as if the amendment or replacement were made by the maker of the secondary legislation (despite section 115(a)).
-- src:817 | Secondary legislation that is amended or replaced by resolution of the House of Representatives may be disallowed as if the amendment or replacement were made by the maker of the secondary legislation (despite section 115(a)).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 119(3) (src:817)
GIVEN `it was amended or replaced by resolution of the House` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is otherwise within the disallowance subpart as if made by its maker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the secondary legislation may be disallowed` `it was amended or replaced by resolution of the House` `it is otherwise within the disallowance subpart as if made by its maker` MEANS
    `it was amended or replaced by resolution of the House` AND `it is otherwise within the disallowance subpart as if made by its maker`

-- (1) The House of Representatives may amend or replace any secondary legislation to which this subpart applies by resolution.
-- src:813 | The House of Representatives may amend or replace any secondary legislation to which this subpart applies by resolution.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 119(1) (src:813)
GIVEN `this subpart applies to the secondary legislation being amended or replaced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the House of Representatives may amend or replace the secondary legislation by resolution` `this subpart applies to the secondary legislation being amended or replaced` MEANS
    `this subpart applies to the secondary legislation being amended or replaced`

§ `Section 120 -- Resolution or motion is secondary legislation`

-- src:819 | A resolution or a motion that (whether itself or as a result of section 117) disallows, amends, or replaces secondary legislation under this subpart is secondary legislation (see Part 3 for publication requirements).
-- src:818 | 120 Resolution or motion is secondary legislation
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 120(1) (src:818) (src:819)
GIVEN `it disallows, amends or replaces secondary legislation under the disallowance subpart, itself or as a result of section 117` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a resolution or a motion is secondary legislation` `it disallows, amends or replaces secondary legislation under the disallowance subpart, itself or as a result of section 117` MEANS
    `it disallows, amends or replaces secondary legislation under the disallowance subpart, itself or as a result of section 117`

-- (3) Sections 116(2) and 117(2) apply even if the copy or notice is not yet published: the day of ceasing to have effect does not wait for publication.
-- src:821 | However, sections 116(2) and 117(2) apply even if the copy or notice is not yet published.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 120(3) (src:821)
GIVEN `the copy or notice is published` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sections 116(2) and 117(2) apply` `the copy or notice is published` MEANS TRUE

-- (2) For that purpose, the Clerk of the House of Representatives must lodge a copy of the resolution or notice of the motion with the PCO, and the PCO must publish it as if it had been drafted by the PCO, under section 69(3).
-- src:820 | For that purpose, the Clerk of the House of Representatives must lodge a copy of the resolution or notice of the motion with the PCO, and the PCO must publish it as if it had been drafted by the PCO, under section 69(3).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 120(2) (src:820)
GIVEN `the resolution or motion disallows, amends or replaces secondary legislation under the disallowance subpart` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Clerk of the House of Representatives must lodge a copy of the resolution or notice of the motion with the PCO` `the resolution or motion disallows, amends or replaces secondary legislation under the disallowance subpart` MEANS
    `the resolution or motion disallows, amends or replaces secondary legislation under the disallowance subpart`

-- src:820 | For that purpose, the Clerk of the House of Representatives must lodge a copy of the resolution or notice of the motion with the PCO, and the PCO must publish it as if it had been drafted by the PCO, under section 69(3).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 120(2) (src:820)
GIVEN `the resolution or motion disallows, amends or replaces secondary legislation under the disallowance subpart` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the PCO must publish the copy or notice as if it had been drafted by the PCO` `the resolution or motion disallows, amends or replaces secondary legislation under the disallowance subpart` MEANS
    `the resolution or motion disallows, amends or replaces secondary legislation under the disallowance subpart`

§ `Section 121 -- Definitions used in this subpart`

-- src:825 | deadline means,—
-- src:826 | for legislation that is made on or after 1 January but before the close of 30 June in the same year, the close of 30 June in the next year:
-- src:827 | for legislation that is made on or after 1 July but before the close of 31 December in the same year, the close of 31 December in the next year
-- "deadline means, for legislation that is made on or after 1 January but before the close of 30 June in the same year, the close of 30 June in the next year; for legislation made on or after 1 July but before the close of 31 December in the same year,
-- the close of 31 December in the next year." Every day of a year falls in one of the two ranges, so the deadline always exists.
-- src:823 | 121 Definitions used in this subpart
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 121, definition of deadline (src:823) (src:825-827)
GIVEN `the day the legislation is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the deadline for confirmation of legislation made on` `the day the legislation is made` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the day the legislation is made` AT MOST 6
    THEN Date 30 6 (DATE_YEAR `the day the legislation is made` PLUS 1)
    ELSE Date 31 12 (DATE_YEAR `the day the legislation is made` PLUS 1)

-- "unconfirmed legislation means legislation that is not confirmed on or before the deadline."
-- src:828 | unconfirmed legislation means legislation that is not confirmed on or before the deadline.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 121, definition of unconfirmed legislation (src:828)
GIVEN `the day the confirming provision commences` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the deadline` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is unconfirmed legislation` `the day the confirming provision commences` `the deadline` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the confirming provision commences`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST commencement THEN commencement GREATER THAN `the deadline`

§ `Section 122 -- What secondary legislation must be confirmed under this subpart`

-- src:829 | 122 What secondary legislation must be confirmed under this subpart
-- src:830 | This subpart applies to secondary legislation if it is made under an empowering provision listed in Schedule 4.
-- src:831 | However, if that schedule limits which matters require confirmation under an empowering provision, this subpart applies to the secondary legislation only if it relates to those confirmable matters.
-- Applies to secondary legislation made under an empowering provision listed in Schedule 4; where Schedule 4 limits which matters require confirmation, only if the legislation relates to those matters.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 122 (src:829) (src:830-831)
GIVEN `it is made under an empowering provision listed in Schedule 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Schedule 4 limits which matters require confirmation under the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it relates to the confirmable matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the confirmation subpart applies to the secondary legislation` `it is made under an empowering provision listed in Schedule 4` `Schedule 4 limits which matters require confirmation under the provision` `it relates to the confirmable matters` MEANS
    `it is made under an empowering provision listed in Schedule 4` AND ((NOT `Schedule 4 limits which matters require confirmation under the provision`) OR `it relates to the confirmable matters`)

§ `Section 123 -- Secondary legislation must be confirmed by deadline (or otherwise will be revoked)`

-- src:832 | 123 Secondary legislation must be confirmed by deadline (or otherwise will be revoked)
-- src:833 | If secondary legislation to which this subpart applies is not confirmed on or before the deadline, the legislation is revoked on the deadline (if it is still in force).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 123 (src:832) (src:833)
GIVEN `the confirmation subpart applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is unconfirmed legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is still in force on the deadline` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the legislation is revoked on the deadline` `the confirmation subpart applies to it` `it is unconfirmed legislation` `it is still in force on the deadline` MEANS
    `the confirmation subpart applies to it` AND `it is unconfirmed legislation` AND `it is still in force on the deadline`

§ `Section 124 -- How to confirm secondary legislation`

-- src:834 | 124 How to confirm secondary legislation
-- src:835 | To confirm secondary legislation by a deadline for the purposes of this subpart,—
-- src:836 | an Act must contain a provision to the effect that it confirms the legislation; and
-- src:837 | the provision must commence on or before the deadline.
-- src:838 | The later repeal of the Act or provision does not affect the confirmation (see section 32, which relates to the effect of repeal).
-- To confirm by a deadline an Act must contain a provision to the effect that it confirms the legislation, and the provision must commence on or before the deadline. The later repeal of the Act or provision does not affect the confirmation (section 32).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 124 (src:834) (src:835-838)
GIVEN `an Act contains a provision to the effect that it confirms the legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the provision commences` IS A DATE
      `the deadline` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the legislation is confirmed by the deadline` `an Act contains a provision to the effect that it confirms the legislation` `the day the provision commences` `the deadline` MEANS
    `an Act contains a provision to the effect that it confirms the legislation` AND (`the day the provision commences` AT MOST `the deadline`)

@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 124(2) (src:838)
GIVEN `the Act or provision is repealed later` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the later repeal affects the confirmation` `the Act or provision is repealed later` MEANS FALSE

§ `Section 125 -- Usual effect of revocation if not confirmed by deadline`

-- The printed item "any duties, levies, or road user charges" is a member, and so is each of the three things it names (ruling C).
DECLARE `Kind of charge` IS ONE OF
    `a duty, levy or road user charge`
    `a duty`
    `a levy`
    `a road user charge`
    `an order made under section 5(1) of the Energy Resources Levy Act 1976`
    `fees or charges to which section 270(4) to (6) of the Land Transport Act 1998 applies`
    `levy rates set by regulations made under section 41(1)(e) of the Waste Minimisation Act 2008`

-- src:841 | any duties, levies, or road user charges imposed under the unconfirmed legislation are cancelled and, if paid, must be refunded (except as set out in subsection (2)); and
-- src:842 | any other legislation that was previously amended, repealed, or revoked by the unconfirmed legislation is restored or revived (as it was immediately before it was amended, repealed, or revoked); and
-- src:843 | the restoration or revival takes effect at the time the unconfirmed legislation is revoked; and
-- src:844 | revocation of the unconfirmed legislation does not otherwise affect its previous operation or anything done or suffered under it.
-- src:845 | Subsection (1)﻿(a) does not apply to any of the following:
-- src:846 | orders made under section 5(1) of the Energy Resources Levy Act 1976; or
-- src:847 | fees or charges to which section 270(4) to (6) of the Land Transport Act 1998 applies; or
-- src:848 | levy rates set by regulations made under section 41(1)﻿(e) of the Waste Minimisation Act 2008.
-- src:849 | However, this section does not apply if the unconfirmed legislation is made under an empowering provision listed in Part 2 of Schedule 4.
-- (1)(a) any duties, levies, or road user charges imposed under the unconfirmed legislation are cancelled and, if paid, must be refunded (except as set out in (2)); (2) subsection (1)(a) does not apply to the three listed kinds;
-- (3) this section does not apply if the legislation is made under an empowering provision listed in Part 2 of Schedule 4 (section 126 applies instead).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 125(1)(a), (2) and (3) (src:841) (src:845-849)
GIVEN charge IS A `Kind of charge`
      `it is made under an empowering provision listed in Part 2 of Schedule 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a charge imposed under the unconfirmed legislation is cancelled and, if paid, refunded` charge `when` `it is made under an empowering provision listed in Part 2 of Schedule 4` MEANS
    IF `it is made under an empowering provision listed in Part 2 of Schedule 4`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER charge
         WHEN `a duty, levy or road user charge` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a duty` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a levy` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a road user charge` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an order made under section 5(1) of the Energy Resources Levy Act 1976` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `fees or charges to which section 270(4) to (6) of the Land Transport Act 1998 applies` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `levy rates set by regulations made under section 41(1)(e) of the Waste Minimisation Act 2008` THEN FALSE

-- (1)(d) revocation of the unconfirmed legislation does not otherwise affect its previous operation or anything done or suffered under it.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 125(1)(d) (src:844)
GIVEN `the revocation of the unconfirmed legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the revocation otherwise affects the previous operation of the unconfirmed legislation` `the revocation of the unconfirmed legislation` MEANS FALSE

-- (1)(c) The restoration or revival takes effect at the time the unconfirmed legislation is revoked (on and from the deadline, section 125(1) lead-in).
-- src:840 | If unconfirmed legislation is revoked by section 123, the following applies on and from the deadline:
-- src:843 | the restoration or revival takes effect at the time the unconfirmed legislation is revoked; and
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 125(1)(c) (src:840) (src:843)
GIVEN `the day the unconfirmed legislation is revoked by section 123` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the restoration or revival takes effect on revocation of unconfirmed legislation` `the day the unconfirmed legislation is revoked by section 123` MEANS
    `the day the unconfirmed legislation is revoked by section 123`

§ `Section 126 -- Effect on some legislation of not being confirmed by deadline (whether or not earlier revoked)`

-- src:850 | 126 Effect on some legislation of not being confirmed by deadline (whether or not earlier revoked)
-- src:851 | This section applies to unconfirmed legislation made under an empowering provision listed in Part 2 of Schedule 4 (whether it is revoked before the deadline or on the deadline by section 123).
-- src:852 | The legislation is taken, on and from the deadline, to have been invalid for any previous period for which it purported to be in force.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 126 (src:850) (src:851-852)
GIVEN `it is unconfirmed legislation made under an empowering provision listed in Part 2 of Schedule 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the legislation is taken to have been invalid, on and from the deadline, for any previous period it purported to be in force` `it is unconfirmed legislation made under an empowering provision listed in Part 2 of Schedule 4` MEANS
    `it is unconfirmed legislation made under an empowering provision listed in Part 2 of Schedule 4`

§ `Section 127 -- Confirmable secondary legislation must state this fact`

-- src:854 | The explanatory note of secondary legislation to which this subpart applies must—
-- src:855 | state (or contain statements to the effect) that the legislation must be confirmed by an Act before the deadline and that, if it is not confirmed, it will be revoked on that deadline; and
-- src:856 | state the deadline.
-- src:853 | 127 Confirmable secondary legislation must state this fact
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 127 (src:853) (src:854-856)
GIVEN `the explanatory note states that the legislation must be confirmed by an Act before the deadline and that if it is not confirmed it will be revoked on that deadline` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the explanatory note states the deadline` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the explanatory note complies with section 127` `the explanatory note states that the legislation must be confirmed by an Act before the deadline and that if it is not confirmed it will be revoked on that deadline` `the explanatory note states the deadline` MEANS
    `the explanatory note states that the legislation must be confirmed by an Act before the deadline and that if it is not confirmed it will be revoked on that deadline` AND `the explanatory note states the deadline`

-- src:857 | However, a failure to include those statements does not affect the validity of the secondary legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 127(2) (src:857)
GIVEN `the explanatory note complies with section 127` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a failure to include the statements affects the validity of the secondary legislation` `the explanatory note complies with section 127` MEANS FALSE
